{#
  Benchmark harness dispatcher -- the single include point op templates use
  (e.g. `{% include "common/standalone/benchmark.j2" %}` in
  ConvolutionFunctions/convolve/convolve.c.j2). Op templates stay agnostic to
  which physical/simulated target is active; they only need to define
  `{{name}}_bench_init()` / `{{name}}_bench_op()` and set
  `supports_benchmark = true` before including common/standalone/main.j2.

  Selects between the two interchangeable backends based on the
  `benchmark_target` context variable, set at generation time:
    - "fvp" (default)  -> benchmark_fvp.j2 (DWT cycle counter only, works on
                           cortex-m4/m55 under FVP or hardware, not cycle
                           accurate on FVP)
    - "hardware"        -> benchmark_hw.j2  (DWT + ARMv8.1-M PMU event
                           counters, Cortex-M55/Apollo510 only)

  Both backends expose the identical `helia_benchmark_run(name, op)` entry
  point and [BENCH]/[PERF] output lines (the hardware backend additionally
  emits [PMU] lines), so main.j2's `{{prefix}}_{{name}}_benchmark_run()` call
  site needs no target-specific logic either.
#}
{% set benchmark_target = benchmark_target | default("fvp") %}
{% if benchmark_target == "hardware" %}
{% include "common/standalone/benchmark_hw.j2" %}
{% else %}
{% include "common/standalone/benchmark_fvp.j2" %}
{% endif %}
